                        ],
                        "form": "den Autoritarismus"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25545b7b-d07f-3892-99e7-91b04e5e8ab7",
                        "entry_id": "49af89f7-984e-3503-b7c8-3015542cd4e9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Anspruch eines Regimes auf absolute Autorität"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88751200-87fc-45ae-bc39-93f80b0a5c0e",
                                "sense_id": "25545b7b-d07f-3892-99e7-91b04e5e8ab7",
                                "text": "„[D]ie chinesische Führung nutzt das Leben der Uiguren als Testlabor für digitalen Autoritarismus. […]“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94817e14-d21f-3a02-9d3e-37e8759db6f3",
                        "entry_id": "49af89f7-984e-3503-b7c8-3015542cd4e9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Eigenschaft, autoritär und herrisch zu sein"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cfc288ff-7a05-4289-817f-d94b3c4c5143",
                        "source_entry_id": "49af89f7-984e-3503-b7c8-3015542cd4e9",
                        "source_sense_id": "25545b7b-d07f-3892-99e7-91b04e5e8ab7",
                        "source_sense_description": "bildungssprachlich, Politik: Anspruch eines Regimes auf absolute Autorität",
                        "target_lang_word": "authoritarianism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "authoritarianism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "139c704e-5223-3077-9df6-7a0f6a977e3b",
                                        "entry_id": "fd09c21b-969f-3343-91e1-f3812ff52474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of government in which the governing body has absolute, or almost absolute, control. Typically this control is maintained by force, and little heed is paid to public opinion or the judicial system."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcef9f57-be03-4551-816f-504fcef0b3a2",
                                                "sense_id": "139c704e-5223-3077-9df6-7a0f6a977e3b",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: dictatorialism; autocratism; totalitarianism (see usage note there)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdcf8499-188d-4ca1-b037-040a4b2abe41",
                                                "sense_id": "139c704e-5223-3077-9df6-7a0f6a977e3b",
                                                "text": "This is the struggle of our time. The forces of freedom, openness and global community against the forces of authoritarianism, isolationism and nationalism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc9011ee-7db6-4e98-80d7-90b18c059c1b",
                                                "sense_id": "139c704e-5223-3077-9df6-7a0f6a977e3b",
                                                "text": "Working from a psycho-dynamic perspective, Fromm explained authoritarianism as a response to the breakdown of traditional social structures brought about by industrialization and modernization."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a656eca-4875-4c16-a43a-8b70f9a1781b",
                                                "sense_id": "139c704e-5223-3077-9df6-7a0f6a977e3b",
                                                "text": "Instead of three co-equal branches acting as a check on each other, power has become increasingly concentrated over the years in the White House – a trend that is now being supercharged under Mr. Trump in ways that, to critics, raise the specter of authoritarianism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20865f37-3183-4d7e-ba57-c8bda73f5383",
                                                "sense_id": "139c704e-5223-3077-9df6-7a0f6a977e3b",
                                                "text": "If Trump defies the Court here, then America will have taken an important step toward authoritarianism and anti-constitutional government."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4eae060-c2bf-49a7-83ab-99f01840b59f",
                        "source_entry_id": "49af89f7-984e-3503-b7c8-3015542cd4e9",
                        "source_sense_id": "25545b7b-d07f-3892-99e7-91b04e5e8ab7",
                        "source_sense_description": "bildungssprachlich, Politik: Anspruch eines Regimes auf absolute Autorität",
                        "target_lang_word": "autoritarisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "autoritarisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5852963b-d7af-3c78-9a66-04250e4dca23",
                                        "entry_id": "e973bab9-8cb0-3c76-8224-a97437c93319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Manière d’agir de ceux qui font de l’autorité le principe de leur action, de leur parole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24e13bae-6b29-47ef-8d5e-87de5cfd71c6",
                                                "sense_id": "5852963b-d7af-3c78-9a66-04250e4dca23",
                                                "text": "Après six mois d’autoritarisme désordonné : procès de presse à tort et à travers, révocations irritantes de fonctionnaires, persécutions de tout ordre, l’entreprise du Seize Mai échouait piteusement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b0949dc-d801-4beb-b2c4-bd949155839b",
                                                "sense_id": "5852963b-d7af-3c78-9a66-04250e4dca23",
                                                "text": "En Allemagne, en France, et même dans l’Angleterre victorienne, la montée de l’autoritarisme familial produit des schizophrènes, des suicidés, des alcooliques. L'éducation devient persécution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f01c143-ff5a-4151-9fa1-f2acb2a8b87f",
                                                "sense_id": "5852963b-d7af-3c78-9a66-04250e4dca23",
                                                "text": "Donald Trump a failli lamentablement, mais il a quand même presque été réélu. On peine à imaginer jusqu’où un leader avec tous ses atouts, l’appui inconditionnel d’un grand parti et avec en prime la compétence, aurait pu – ou pourrait un jour – mener les États-Unis dans la voie vers l’autoritarisme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4e71ea54-e751-4686-90db-2f2131938922",
                        "source_entry_id": "49af89f7-984e-3503-b7c8-3015542cd4e9",
